]]]></Value>
    </codeType>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EExtensions \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Eremain subordinate and proportionate to the original building in both scale and form by ensuring that: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eall extensions step down by at least 0.5 metres from the roofline of the original building \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eside extensions are also set back a minimum of 0.5 metres from the front elevation of the original building \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ea minimum 1 metre gap is maintained between the extension and the side boundary of the plot to allow for access, enable future maintenance and prevent a \u2018terracing effect\u2019 \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EException:\u003C/strong\u003E Deviation from these standards may be acceptable where a proposal clearly responds to the unique characteristics of the site or local context. Any such proposals will be considered by the Council on a case-by-case basis.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
    <developmentScales>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "Householder Applications"
]]]></Value>
    </developmentScales>
